35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The total time for a full pass is about 102 minutes. However, an outside firm requires us to tidy up first, which means we wouldn't be fully removing the labor. What did the rest of you find?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It's just as I thought! Some of us are barely here, and only a few people are actually making the kitchen messy. It doesn't feel fair to split everything equally when the usage is so different.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems our conflicts stem from reminders about unfinished tasks. Interestingly, the previous tenants tried permanent assignments, but it led to them barely speaking. We must be careful not to sacrifice our relationships for the sake of a schedule.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The money is a mess! We're buying the same spray twice and spending 2,300 yen a month on supplies. Also, the office cleaner costs 4,200 yen an hour and one person has to collect all the money!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found out that we all have different ideas of what ""done"" means, which is why the rooms change so much. Also, the bathroom grout gets dirty again in just eleven days because of the poor ventilation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, if the bathroom degrades in eleven days regardless of effort, a strict rota might just lead to frustration. @Victoria, the previous tenants' failure suggests that permanent ownership can create resentment. We need a balanced approach.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! If some people are barely here and others do all the cooking, a fixed rota is just unfair. We need a system that reflects how we actually live, not just a piece of paper.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, while I understand your point about fairness, we must consider the emotional cost. If we create a system based on usage, we might spend more time monitoring each other than actually cleaning. That is a recipe for more conflict.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But we're already wasting money by buying things twice! If we hire a cleaner, we need a way to pay them that isn't a headache for one person. We need a plan for the money too!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the ""done"" part is the biggest problem. If we don't agree on a standard, we'll just keep arguing, no matter who is assigned to the room. It's scary to think we're all seeing different things.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, you're right. Without a shared standard, any system will fail. However, we must also consider the time. 102 minutes is significant. If we hire a firm, we still have to tidy, which adds to that time.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But if we just stick to a rota, the people who are always here will feel like they're doing all the work for people who aren't even around! That's not a shared standard, that's just unfair.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, fairness is subjective, but resentment is universal. If we focus too much on who uses what, we risk turning our home into a ledger of debts. We need a solution that minimizes friction.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I think we should just pay for a cleaner! It stops the fighting about who did what, and we can just split the cost. We just need a better way to handle the money!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Rin that a cleaner might stop the fighting. If we have a professional, maybe the ""done"" standard will finally be the same for everyone, and I won't have to worry so much.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"If we hire a professional, we solve the standard of ""done"" and the time burden, but we must address the payment logistics and the tidying requirement. It seems the most rational way to avoid long-term conflict.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still worried about the fairness of the cost if some of us aren't even here! But if it stops the fighting and the confusion over who's doing what, maybe it's the only way we'll all stay happy.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"If we can agree on a fair way to handle the payments, a professional service seems the safest path. It removes the personal friction of reminders and the risk of permanent resentment.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"Yay! I'm so glad we're agreeing! As long as we make a super clear rule about how to pay so nobody is stuck paying for everyone else, a cleaner sounds like the best idea!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel a lot better if we can just have a professional do it. It would be so much easier not to worry about the state of the bathroom every time I go in.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
